<title>SINGAPORE: FJ Benjamin incorporates U.S. unit.</title>
<headline>FJ Benjamin incorporates U.S. unit.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Luxury fashion retailer FJ Benjamin Holdings Ltd said on Monday it has incorporated a U.S. subsidiary, Ferro Designs (US) Inc, to operate a design studio and source materials for the group.</p>
<p>The move followed F J's decision to relocate its design studio to New York from Sydney, Australia, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>FJ's shares were sold down recently following a 29.7 percent fall in net profit to Singapore $3.72 million for its first half ended December 31 1996. The company said its performance was affected by its Australian operations.</p>
<p>At 0655 GMT, the shares were trading around Singapore $0.865, up S$0.025 from Friday at 0655 GMT. Volume was an active 1.92 million units.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
